        "reason": "Adds p/swift to the default Semgrep registry packs. Swift CodeQL needs a macOS runner; callers may waive it (codeql_waive_languages), and Semgrep then has to actually cover Swift code."
      },
      {
        "path": ".github/actions/sast-semgrep/action.yml",
        "from_sha256": "067fd83421e09302ee3b227d0e6f01a20e4ae30bc01608ed77d05bc66ab88ac4",
        "to_sha256": "f383ae5238f15e8485924a491b8a4599ccd110dd95add5fa305c71b405f02edb",
        "reason": "Status followed the scanner's exit code, so exit 1 (any finding, even low or info) was FAIL. That ignored the policy's fail_on severities (release-policy.yml: semgrep critical/high, bandit high, shellcheck high) and bypassed reviewed accepted findings, which apply in count_blocking.py. Exit 0/1 now goes through count_blocking at the policy severities; any other exit, or a parse error, stays TOOL_FAILURE."
